course: dictionary
lesson: 1338
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer means. Camomile is a good example. It can be a small plant with daisy-like flowers, a drink made from those flowers, or an old medicine.
explain: «Alice's new rule: pepper makes people hot-tempered, vinegar sour, camomile bitter, and barley-sugar makes children sweet-tempered.» Camomile sits in a list of tastes, next to sour and sweet, so here it means a bitter taste, not a flower.
explain: Always test your meaning. Put the meaning you have chosen in place of the word and check that the sentence still makes sense. If it does not, try another meaning.
fact: Camomile is a noun, and it is uncountable, so we say some camomile, not a camomile.
fact: Camomile is also spelled chamomile.
fact: Camomile can mean a small plant with white petals around a yellow middle, and a sweet, apple-like smell.
fact: Camomile tea is made from dried flowers, and people often drink it to feel calm or sleepy.
fact: Long ago, camomile was used to make a bitter medicine.
exercise: Alice says camomile is bitter. What does camomile mean here? | *A bitter drink or medicine made from the plant | A kind of hard sweet | A pet rabbit | A small plant with tiny daisy-like flowers
exercise: Mum makes camomile tea before bed. What does camomile mean in this sentence? | A plant with white petals | A type of biscuit | *A drink made from dried flowers | A bitter medicine from long ago
exercise: Find and copy one word from «barley-sugar makes children sweet-tempered» that means a hard sweet. | sweet-tempered | *barley-sugar | makes | children
test: The camomile in the garden had tiny white petals and a yellow middle. What does camomile mean here? | A sweet, like barley-sugar | A cup of tea at bedtime | *A plant with daisy-like flowers | A bitter taste
test: Which other spelling of camomile is also correct? | Chamber | *Chamomile | Cinnamon | Camel
exam: «Camomile bitter» is in a list of tastes. Which meaning fits best, and why? | A sweet, because barley-sugar is a sweet | *A bitter taste, because the words around it name tastes | A cuddly toy, because children like soft things | A flower, because the sentence is about a garden
